{
  "id": "p6",
  "title": "while, repeat and case",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p6-l1",
      "title": "while … do",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "while condition do statement repeats as long as the condition is true. It checks first, so if the condition is false from the start, the loop doesn't run at all.",
        "Something inside the loop must change the condition, or it runs forever.",
        "Use while when you don't know in advance how many rounds you'll need."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Double;",
          "var",
          "  n, steps: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  n := 1;",
          "  steps := 0;",
          "  while n < 1000 do",
          "  begin",
          "    n := n * 2;",
          "    steps := steps + 1;",
          "  end;",
          "  writeln('After ', steps, ' doublings: ', n);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "After 10 doublings: 1024"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p6-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When does a while loop check its condition?",
          "options": [
            "Before every round",
            "After every round",
            "Only once",
            "Never"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "If it's false at the start, the body never runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Grow;",
            "var",
            "  n: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 1;",
            "  while n < 50 do",
            "    n := n * 2;",
            "  writeln(n);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "64",
            "32",
            "128",
            "6"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "n doubles until it's no longer below 50: 1, 2, 4 … 32, 64."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l1-e3",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program never ends. Which line is missing something?",
          "code": [
            "program Forever;",
            "var",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  i := 1;",
            "  while i <= 3 do",
            "    writeln(i);",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "Nothing changes i. The body should be begin writeln(i); i := i + 1 end."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l1-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Keep going while the number is above 0.",
          "code": [
            "  while n > 0 ___",
            "    n := n div 10;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "do",
            "then",
            "loop",
            "begin"
          ],
          "answer": "do",
          "explanation": "while … do."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l1-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Digits;",
            "var",
            "  n, count: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 1972;",
            "  count := 0;",
            "  while n > 0 do",
            "  begin",
            "    n := n div 10;",
            "    count := count + 1;",
            "  end;",
            "  writeln(count);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "4",
            "3",
            "1972",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1972 → 197 → 19 → 1 → 0: four divisions, one for every digit."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When is while better than for?",
          "options": [
            "When you don't know beforehand how many rounds you need",
            "Always",
            "When counting from 1 to 10",
            "Never"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "for is for a known number of rounds."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6-l2",
      "title": "repeat … until",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "repeat … until condition runs the body first and checks afterwards, so it always runs at least once. It stops when the condition becomes true (the opposite of while).",
        "Between repeat and until you can write several statements without begin … end.",
        "It's perfect for asking again until the answer is valid."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Ask;",
          "var",
          "  n: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  repeat",
          "    write('Pick 1 to 10: ');",
          "    readln(n);",
          "  until (n >= 1) and (n <= 10);",
          "  writeln('Thanks, you picked ', n);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Pick 1 to 10: 0",
          "Pick 1 to 10: 42",
          "Pick 1 to 10: 7",
          "Thanks, you picked 7"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "0",
          "42",
          "7"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p6-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How often does a repeat loop run at least?",
          "options": [
            "Once",
            "Never",
            "Twice",
            "It depends on the condition only"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The condition is checked at the end."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When does repeat … until stop?",
          "options": [
            "When the condition becomes true",
            "When the condition becomes false",
            "After 10 rounds",
            "Never"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "while runs WHILE true; repeat runs UNTIL true."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Finish the loop.",
          "code": [
            "  repeat",
            "    n := n - 3;",
            "  ___ n < 0;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "until",
            "while",
            "end",
            "do"
          ],
          "answer": "until",
          "explanation": "repeat … until condition."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Rep;",
            "var",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  i := 1;",
            "  repeat",
            "    writeln(i);",
            "    i := i + 1;",
            "  until i > 3;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "1\n2\n3",
            "1\n2",
            "1",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "i goes 1, 2, 3; after printing 3, i becomes 4 and the loop stops."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Once;",
            "begin",
            "  repeat",
            "    writeln('once');",
            "  until true;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "once",
            "nothing",
            "once\nonce",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The condition is already true, but repeat runs the body once before checking."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Do the statements between repeat and until need begin … end?",
          "options": [
            "No, repeat and until already group them",
            "Yes, always",
            "Only if there are more than two",
            "Only in Turbo Pascal"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "repeat … until works like begin … end."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6-l3",
      "title": "case … of",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "case picks one of several branches by value: case day of 1: …; 2: …; end; Values can be lists (1, 7:) and ranges (2..6:). else catches everything else.",
        "case works with integers, chars and other countable (ordinal) types, but not with strings or reals.",
        "It's much tidier than a long chain of if … else if."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Days;",
          "var",
          "  day: integer;",
          "  grade: char;",
          "begin",
          "  day := 6;",
          "  case day of",
          "    1, 7: writeln('Weekend');",
          "    2..6: writeln('Work day');",
          "  else",
          "    writeln('No such day');",
          "  end;",
          "  grade := 'B';",
          "  case grade of",
          "    'A': writeln('Excellent');",
          "    'B', 'C': writeln('Good');",
          "    'D'..'F': writeln('Practice more');",
          "  end;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Work day",
          "Good"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p6-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which types can case use?",
          "options": [
            "Integers, chars and other ordinal types",
            "Strings",
            "Reals",
            "Any type"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Not strings or reals: Turbo Pascal stops with Type mismatch."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Sz;",
            "var",
            "  n: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 5;",
            "  case n of",
            "    1..3: writeln('small');",
            "    4..7: writeln('medium');",
            "    8..10: writeln('big');",
            "  end;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "medium",
            "small",
            "big",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "5 is in the range 4..7."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Catch every other value.",
          "code": [
            "  case n of",
            "    1: writeln('one');",
            "    2: writeln('two');",
            "  ___",
            "    writeln('many');",
            "  end;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "else",
            "default:",
            "otherwise:",
            "others"
          ],
          "answer": "else",
          "explanation": "else (Turbo Pascal also accepts otherwise)."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l3-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Menu;",
            "var",
            "  choice: string;",
            "begin",
            "  choice := 'save';",
            "  case choice of",
            "    'save': writeln('Saved');",
            "  end;",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "case can't use a string. Use a char (like 's') or if … else if."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l3-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Vow;",
            "var",
            "  c: char;",
            "begin",
            "  c := 'e';",
            "  case c of",
            "    'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u': writeln('vowel');",
            "  else",
            "    writeln('consonant');",
            "  end;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "vowel",
            "consonant",
            "nothing",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "'e' is in the list of vowels."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How do you write \"2 to 6\" as a case label?",
          "options": [
            "2..6:",
            "2-6:",
            "2 to 6:",
            "[2,6]:"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Two dots make a range."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
